@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Customer journey 3: authenticate to storage and upload/download job files
actor "Customer CLI / SDK" as C
boundary "Public API / S3\nNGINX edge" as E
participant "Gateway\ncredential helper" as W
participant "MinIO STS / S3\non GCP VM" as M
participant "MinIO identity plugin\nlocal authentication" as I
participant "Supabase\nJWT / API-key authority" as A
database "GCP VM disk\nMinIO objects" as D

opt Credential helper used (direct STS is also possible)
C -[#16803C]> E : [ENC] HTTPS: authenticate / request storage credentials
E -[#DC2626]> W : [PLAIN] Internal HTTP to Gateway
W -[#D4A000]> M : [CHECK] Request STS credentials on customer's behalf\nCapture effective helper-to-STS URL and routing
end
opt Direct STS exchange
C -[#16803C]> E : [ENC] HTTPS: STS exchange with caller token
E -[#DC2626]> M : [PLAIN] Internal HTTP to MinIO
end
M -[#DC2626]> I : [PLAIN] Local HTTP identity-plugin call
I -[#16803C]> A : [ENC] HTTPS: validate JWT / look up API key
A -[#16803C]> I : [ENC] HTTPS identity response
I -[#DC2626]> M : [PLAIN] Local HTTP authorization / session policy response
note over I,A
JWT is validated upstream, not just parsed.
API-key expiry and session lifetime/revocation have gaps (F04).
Plugin permits up to one year; not every issued session lasts a year.
end note
M -[#DC2626]> E : [PLAIN] STS credential response: HTTP backend;\nhelper path may also traverse Gateway
E -[#16803C]> C : [ENC] HTTPS: temporary storage credentials
group Upload inputs / download outputs
C -[#16803C]> E : [ENC] HTTPS: signed S3 PUT / GET with tenant credentials
E -[#DC2626]> M : [PLAIN] HTTP: object content and request metadata
M -[#DC2626]> M : [PLAIN] Object bytes readable to MinIO process
M -[#16803C]> D : [ENC] GCP storage-layer encryption at rest
note over M,D
No enforced MinIO SSE/KMS or customer-only encryption established.
Disk encryption does not hide objects from MinIO/admins.
STS policy enforcement also requires the MinIO fix (F03).
end note
D -[#DC2626]> M : [PLAIN] Transparent disk decryption returns readable bytes\nLocal application read, not a plaintext network claim
M -[#DC2626]> E : [PLAIN] HTTP: download body / upload acknowledgement
E -[#16803C]> C : [ENC] HTTPS: file or acknowledgement
end
@enduml
